# PROJECT RULES — Hospital Maintenance System

These rules are effective immediately. Do NOT override without explicit user approval.

---

## GIT — Strictly Prohibited

- Never run `git restore` under any circumstances — no exceptions
- Never run `git reset --hard`
- Never run `git clean`
- Never run `git push --force` or `git push -f`
- Never commit, push, pull, merge, or rebase without explicit instruction from the user
- If an undo is needed, notify the user and wait for their command

---

## .ENV and Secret Keys — Strictly Prohibited

- Never read, display, or copy any value from `.env` files
- Never expose API Keys, Secrets, Passwords, or Tokens in any form
- When constructing URLs, use variable names only — e.g. `${APP_URL}` — never the actual value
- If `.env` content must be shown, mask all values — e.g. `APP_KEY=***hidden***`
- Never create or modify `.env` files without explicit instruction

---

## Scope of Work

- Only perform actions that have been explicitly requested
- Never modify files outside the scope of the current task
- If you notice code outside the current scope that should be improved, **report it** to the user — do not change it
- Never delete files or code without user confirmation

---

## Database & Migrations

- Never run `migrate:fresh`, `migrate:reset`, or `db:wipe`
- Always show new Migration code to the user for review before applying
- Never modify migration files that have already been migrated

---

## Best Practices

- Always notify the user before modifying any critical file
- When requirements are unclear, ask first — never assume
- **Parallel Running only** — create new Services separately; never delete legacy code until explicitly confirmed by the user
